{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>A land of wheat and barley</b> — Ten words in the verse. Therefore one must place ten fingers on the bread at the time of blessing. And additionally, corresponding to the ten commandments that apply to bread: kilayim (not sowing mixed species), kilayim (not plowing with mixed species), leket (gleanings), shikhchah (forgotten sheaves), pe'ah (corner of the field), lo techasem (not muzzling the ox), terumah, ma'aser rishon, ma'aser sheni, and challah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:10.785171542Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}